  "text": "ชัน Let's denote the given expression as $a, b, c, d$. The expression can be rearranged as $\\arccos \\cos \\alpha, \\arccos \\cos 3\\alpha, \\arccos \\cos 11\\alpha, \\arccos \\cos t\\alpha$. These expressions should form an arithmetic progression (AP).\n\nFor $a, b, c, d$ to form an AP, the following condition must be satisfied:\n\\[ \\frac{b - a}{2} = \\frac{c - b}{2} = \\frac{d - c}{2} = r, \\]\nwhere $r$ is the common difference.\n\nSo we need to calculate:\n\\[ \\arccos(\\cos \\alpha), \\ \\arccos(\\cos 3\\alpha), \\ \\arccos(\\cos 11\\alpha), \\ \\arccos(\\cos t\\alpha). \\]\n\nSince $\\arccos(\\cos \\theta) = \\theta$ if $\\theta$ is between $0$ and $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ (or $2\\pi$ minus any full rotation), we get:\n\\[ \\arccos(\\cos \\alpha) = \\alpha \\text{ if } \\alpha \\in \\left[0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right] \\text{ or } \\left[2k\\pi, 2\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right], k \\in \\mathbb{Z}. \\]\n\\[ \\arccos(\\cos 3\\alpha) = 3\\alpha \\text{ if } 3\\alpha \\in \\left[0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right] \\text{ or } \\left[2k\\pi, 2\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right], k \\in \\mathbb{Z}. \\]\n\\[ \\arccos(\\cos 11\\alpha) = 11\\alpha \\text{ if } 11\\alpha \\in \\left[0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right] \\text{ or } \\left[2k\\pi, 2\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right], k \\in \\mathbb{Z}. \\]\n\nGiven that $0 < \\alpha < \\pi$, we can say $\\alpha \\in (0, \\pi/2)$, and thus $3\\alpha$ will also be in $(0, 3\\pi/2)$, and similarly for $11\\alpha$. We need to find $\\alpha$ such that:\n\\[ (3\\alpha - \\alpha) / 2 = (11\\alpha - 3\\alpha) / 2 = (t\\alpha - 11\\alpha) / 2. \\]\n\\[ \\alpha / 2 = 4\\alpha / 2 = (t\\alpha - 11\\alpha) / 2. \\]\n\\[ \\alpha / 2 = 2\\alpha. \\]\n\\[ \\alpha / 2 = 2\\alpha / 2. \\]\n\\[ \\alpha = 4\\alpha / 2. \\]\n\\[ \\alpha = t\\alpha / 2 - 11\\alpha / 2. \\]\n\\[ 2 = t - 11. \\]\n\\[ t = 13. \\]\n\nHowever, the simplest way is to just check for the least positive value. The simplest case when $\\alpha = 1$ satisfies the arithmetic progression condition, we can just check. \n\nSo the least positive value of $t$ is 13.\n\nLet's verify:\n\n\\[\\arccos(\\cos \\alpha) = \\alpha, \\ \\arccos(\\cos 3\\alpha) = 3\\alpha \\text{ when } 0 < \\alpha < \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\ \\arccos(\\cos 11\\alpha) = 11\\alpha \\text{ when } 0 < \\alpha < \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\ \\arccos(\\cos 13\\alpha) = 13\\alpha \\text{ for } 0 < \\alpha < \\frac{\\pi}{2}.\\]\n\nSince $0 < 3\\alpha - \\alpha < \\pi$ and $0 < 11\\alpha - 3\\alpha < \\pi$, they should form an arithmetic progression when $\\alpha$ is the smallest positive value in the interval, which is 1. \n\nSo we can conclude the final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{13}\\]",
